export anchor MosaicStyle:
    number: 151
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Mosaic
    idea: The dashboard is laid as a floor mosaic, where small stone tesserae set in pale grout form the totals, the progress of each project and one tile for every task completed in the chart.
    base: light
    palette:
        grout: #d8d0bf, the page, gaps between tiles and panel borders
        panel: #f7f1e4, panels, fields and the chart ground
        creamTile: #efe6d2, background tesserae and empty progress tiles
        sandTile: #e3d3b0, scattered background tesserae and the current tab
        slate: #36506a, progress tiles, last week tiles, one figure and the focus outline
        terracotta: #a4452a, the primary button and this week tiles
        ochre: #b98326, border waves and the outer focus halo, never text
        olive: #55662e, one figure and On track
        basalt: #2a2723, text, outlines and one figure
        muted: #58524a, meta and day labels
        oxideRed: #8c2a1e, overdue and Behind
        amber: #7a5200, At risk
    type:
        Headings use Cochin, Constantia, Sitka Heading, Iowan Old Style,
        Georgia, serif in bold, panel titles in small caps. Text uses
        system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Noto Sans, sans-serif. Greeting 44px,
        panel titles 24px, row titles 17px bold, body 16px at 1.5, meta 13
        to 14px. The totals are never set in type, they are drawn in a 5
        by 7 tessera font at 10px per tile.
    layout:
        A floor of small cream tiles in grout behind everything, up to
        1260px. Every panel is an emblema with a 2px basalt line, a 6px
        grout band and an inner basalt line. The header holds a nine tile
        brand mark, small caps brand, nav with an outlined sand current
        item, a square search, a terracotta button, a square bell and a
        round tile cluster avatar, closed by a three row tessera band of
        basalt and an ochre, cream and terracotta wave. The top row pairs
        the greeting panel, with date and an outlined red notice naming 4
        overdue tasks, with four small emblemata, each with a label, the
        figure laid in tesserae, slate, olive, oxide red or basalt on
        cream tiles, and a short note such as running now. Projects list
        name, category and due date, a bar of twenty tiles where each
        slate tile is 5 percent, percent and tasks, and the status. The
        chart lays two tiles per row and one row per task, slate last week
        and terracotta this week, with values above. Activity spans the
        width in three columns led by small rotated tiles, closed by
        another tessera band. On phones panels stack and totals go two by
        two.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between panels, 12 by 20px rows, tiles on a 10 to 12px grid with about 1.6px grout.
    density: Medium to dense. Many small tiles with calm text around them.
    corners: Nearly square. Tiles 1.2px, controls 3px, the avatar is a round tile cluster.
    borders: Emblema frames of basalt, grout and basalt, and tessera bands of basalt and ochre wave under the header and feed.
    shadows: None. Depth comes from grout and tiles each rotated a few degrees with slightly varied size and colour.
    icons:
        Simple line icons for tools and tessera shapes for markers. Status
        uses a round tile for On track, a triangular tile for At risk and
        a square tile with a hole for Behind, beside the word.
    focus: A 3px slate outline offset 2px inside a 6px ochre halo.
    tone: Plain and craft minded, such as one tile per 5% and One row of tiles per task.
